       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. rotational-cipher.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-KEY PIC 9(2).
       01 WS-TEXT PIC X(128).
       01 WS-CIPHER.
         05 WS-CIPHERLETTER PIC X(1) OCCURS 128 TIMES.

       01 WS-ALPHABET VALUE "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ".
          05 WS-ALPHABETLETTER PIC X(1) OCCURS 26 TIMES INDEXED BY I.

       01 WS-ROTATIONALVALUE PIC 9(2).
       01 WS-DIVISOR PIC 9(2).
       01 WS-ALPHABETPOSITION PIC 9(2).
       01 WS-ITERATOR PIC 9(3).

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       ROTATIONAL-CIPHER.

       MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(WS-TEXT) TO WS-TEXT

       MOVE WS-TEXT TO WS-CIPHER

       DIVIDE WS-KEY BY 26 GIVING WS-DIVISOR REMAINDER WS-ROTATIONALVALUE

       IF NOT WS-ROTATIONALVALUE = 0
          MOVE 1 TO WS-ITERATOR
          PERFORM MOVEALETTER UNTIL WS-ITERATOR = 128.

       MOVEALETTER.       
       SET I TO 1
       SEARCH WS-ALPHABETLETTER
       WHEN WS-ALPHABETLETTER(I)=WS-CIPHERLETTER(WS-ITERATOR)
          MOVE I TO WS-ALPHABETPOSITION
          PERFORM MOVEALETTER2
       END-SEARCH.
      
       ADD 1 TO WS-ITERATOR.

       MOVEALETTER2.
       ADD WS-ROTATIONALVALUE TO WS-ALPHABETPOSITION
      * Catch looping back round i.e ROT1 Z->A
       DIVIDE WS-ALPHABETPOSITION BY 26 GIVING WS-DIVISOR REMAINDER WS-ALPHABETPOSITION

       IF WS-ALPHABETPOSITION=0 THEN
          MOVE 26 TO WS-ALPHABETPOSITION.
      * Shift it back - mod division means 26 -> 0 - but index starts at 1
      
       MOVE WS-ALPHABETLETTER(WS-ALPHABETPOSITION) TO WS-CIPHERLETTER(WS-ITERATOR).

      